ssor strings such as AUTHORITY_ADMISSIBLE or AUTHORITY_ESTABLISHED MUST NOT open the prover by themselves. The immutable 16-atom method profile MUST NOT be rewritten under the same identity. Any capacity increase MUST be represented as a first-class conservative extension proving identical results over the old supported domain, preservation of the issued question's logical semantics, and capacity for the exact resolved bridge-aware theorem. The prover MUST remain blocked until endpoint semantic identity, role binding, derived-atom provenance, authority lineage, conservative capacity extension, same-question preservation, bridge-aware extended capacity, and all inherited semantic-closure obligations are admissible.","forbidden_shortcuts":["any shortcut forbidden by the exact content-identified v1.0.16 predecessor release gate","binding a PREDECESSOR_ATOM to a semantic identity different from the canonical predecessor formula binding","binding a TARGET_ATOM to a semantic identity different from the canonical target formula binding","relabeling a predecessor atom as a target atom or a target atom as a predecessor atom","declaring a BRIDGE_DERIVED_ATOM whose atom ID collides with either endpoint namespace","using a BRIDGE_DERIVED_ATOM without a separately content-identified derivation object","opening semantic authority gates because a successor object merely states AUTHORITY_ADMISSIBLE, AUTHORITY_ESTABLISHED, or DUAL_IDENTITY_ESTABLISHED","mutating max_atoms or solver semantics under the immutable v1.8 entailment-method profile identity","changing the issued entailment question to escape the old method capacity boundary","claiming conservative capacity extension without replayed result equivalence on the old supported domain","claiming bridge-aware capacity from the historical 18-atom count instead of the exact resolved P union B union T theorem"]}
